90
00:04:35,054 --> 00:04:40,095
The way to do that today is to expose the
platform to agents through an MCP server.

91
00:04:41,148 --> 00:04:43,218
MCP stands for Model Context Protocol.

92
00:04:43,236 --> 00:04:46,919
In plain words, it's a standard way
for any agent to ask a system what

93
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:48,823
it knows and what it can do for you.

94
00:04:49,857 --> 00:04:51,683
And one thing stays fixed.

95
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:57,233
People stay at the gate Once the
platform is an MCP server, agents

96
00:04:57,234 --> 00:04:59,334
can find the rules at design time.

97
00:04:59,518 --> 00:05:00,720
What do I mean by this?

98
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:06,331
So before the coding begins, let
me walk you through the life cycle.

99
00:05:06,377 --> 00:05:11,201
At design and build, the team agents ask
the platform how to adopt it and get an

100
00:05:11,201 --> 00:05:13,188
