00:06:00,085 --> 00:06:01,733
and it's exactly the reverse, right?

113
00:06:02,061 --> 00:06:05,956
So the design team, they don't
need to be aware of this.

114
00:06:06,396 --> 00:06:10,600
Once agent comes into the picture,
it already knows through this geo

115
00:06:10,601 --> 00:06:15,415
expansion platform, hey, the layouts
functionally like this in China, and

116
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:17,251
it takes care of it from day one.

117
00:06:17,702 --> 00:06:18,962
And nothing breaks at QA.

118
00:06:18,977 --> 00:06:23,941
There are no confusion or no chaos when
things are being tested against, KYC

119
00:06:23,941 --> 00:06:30,251
or KYB, for an address, for a merchant
or a consumer So there are three,

120
00:06:30,864 --> 00:06:32,565
really three things we need to ask.

121
00:06:32,566 --> 00:06:37,270
And if you remember one slide from
this section, make it this one.

122
00:06:38,075 --> 00:06:43,024
Any platform can give agents three
kinds of tools, and this is--

123
00:06:43,053 --> 00:06:45,397
these are the things I came across.

124
00:06:45,402 --> 00:06:49,137
It can change based on the kind
of platform you own or you run.

125
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:52,823
But the first one that comes to
my mind is: How do I build on this

126
00:06:52,859 --> 00:06:54,645
or move to the current version?

127
00:06:54,649 --> 00:07:00,515
So because, this would solve
for any teams that need the new

128
00:07:00,515 --> 00:07:03,909
updates from you, and that is the
bread and butter for any platform.

129
00:07:04,726 --> 00:07:05,928
The second one is update.

130
00:07:06,245 --> 00:07:08,592
What change that affects my flow?

131
00:07:09,015 --> 00:07:12,871
So that's how a new rule, like
