00:07:37,977 --> 00:07:40,248
I would love to connect
and learn more on that.

139
00:07:42,102 --> 00:07:47,037
So these are the three tools that can
form the backbone or the basis of any

140
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:52,535
platform MCP server Now, what happens
when agents become your customer?

141
00:07:53,143 --> 00:07:58,439
So far, I've talked about a team's
agent, but something bigger happens

142
00:07:58,453 --> 00:08:00,403
once your platform speaks MCP.

143
00:08:01,493 --> 00:08:03,293
Agents become your consumer.

144
00:08:03,494 --> 00:08:07,587
Agents from other systems that
have nothing to do with your team

145
00:08:07,604 --> 00:08:09,826
start asking your platform first.

146
00:08:11,485 --> 00:08:12,924
Let me show you two actually.

147
00:08:13,925 --> 00:08:15,884
The first one is a design agent.

148
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:18,472
Here's the old way.

149
00:08:18,654 --> 00:08:22,391
A designer works in their home
market, the same example, but let's

150
00:08:22,392 --> 00:08:25,997
look at it a different way, and
copies the layout to other markets.

151
00:08:25,999 --> 00:08:26,321
Okay?

152
00:08:26,710 --> 00:08:30,499
So production renders each market
correctly because platform handles it.

153
00:08:30,999 --> 00:08:36,381
QA compares production to the design
files, finds mismatch, and nobody

154
00:08:36,454 --> 00:08:39,577
